  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Prove that\n$$\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}=\\tan\\theta.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\tan\\theta$.\n\nUse double-angle identities, then factor and cancel the common factors.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\frac{1-2\\sin^2\\theta-(1-2\\sin^2 2\\theta)}{\\sin 2\\theta+2\\sin 2\\theta\\cos 2\\theta}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\frac{-2\\sin^2\\theta+2\\sin^2 2\\theta}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta(1+2\\cos 2\\theta)}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\frac{-2\\sin^2\\theta+2(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)^2}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\bigl(1+2(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)\\bigr)}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\frac{2\\sin^2\\theta(4\\cos^2\\theta-1)}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta(4\\cos^2\\theta-1)}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos 2\\theta-\\cos 4\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta+\\sin 4\\theta}&=\\tan\\theta.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe identity holds wherever the original quotient is defined.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
